# Class -> Rust path glob (relative to `crates/freerouting/src`) map for scripts/audit-port.sh's
# per-class matching. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. A class whose Rust home
# spans more than one file gets one map line per file — not one line with several space-separated
# globs, which the reader (`read -r cls path`) would only keep the first token of.
#
# CREATED AND SEEDED BY PLAN 8 TASK 0. Filled by Tasks 5, 6, 7, 11 and 12; **closed by Task 14**,
# which must reach zero `MISSING` and zero `UNMAPPED` on all three invocations below.
#
# ── The three invocations this map serves (plan §The audit, Task 14) ────────────────────────────
#
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh api/mcp crates/freerouting/src '*.java'          scripts/audit-map/freerouting.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh logger  crates/freerouting/src '*.java'          scripts/audit-map/freerouting.map
#   ./scripts/audit-port.sh .       crates/freerouting/src 'Freerouting.java' scripts/audit-map/freerouting.map
#
# If the last one's `.` subpath does not work with the script's argument shape, **read
# `scripts/audit-port.sh` and use the shape it actually accepts** — do not weaken the check to
# make it pass (plan §The audit, Task 14, verbatim).
#
# ── Which task owes which rows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Task 0  — nothing but this file. `crates/freerouting/src` is still Plan 1's stub; every row
#             below is therefore an obligation, and every one of them reports `MISSING` today.
#             That is deliberate: the map records the obligation before the code exists, which is
#             the same shape `scripts/audit-map/fr-router.map` was seeded in.
#   Task 5  — `main.rs`, `cli.rs`, `legacy.rs`, `logging.rs`: the exit ladder, the legacy shim
#             (bug-for-bug, ruling AR), the native subcommand form, the log message set.
#   Task 6  — `commands/route.rs`: `Freerouting.initializeCli`'s real body.
#   Task 7  — `commands/drc.rs`: `initializeDrc`'s real body.
#   Task 11 — `mcp/{jsonrpc,server,stdio}.rs`: the native stdio JSON-RPC transport (ruling AO).
#   Task 12 — `mcp/tools/*`, `commands/info.rs`.
#   Task 14 — closes every remaining row to zero.
#
# ── Two whole packages are rostered, not ported ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `api/mcp/**` (11 files, 2 105 lines) — ruling AO. The port's MCP is spec §13's four tools over a
# native stdio JSON-RPC server, not Java's OpenAPI-derived registry over Jetty/WebSocket. These
# rows are expected to report `ROSTERED`; the roster itself is at the foot of
# `crates/fr-core/src/lib.rs`, so the markers Task 11/12 must carry in **this** crate are the
# `// renamed:` lines that name where each Java capability went.
#
# `logger/**` (7 files) — spec §2 drops `FRLogger` and the log files entirely. Quirk label AI is
# the divergence that survives: Java's Console appender targets `SYSTEM_OUT` and triplicates
# `ERROR`, and the port sends everything to **stderr** through `tracing`; `p8t1`'s `normalize_log`
# merges Java's two streams so the comparison is still a comparison.
# ================================================================================================

# ── Freerouting.java ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One class, five Rust homes. `Freerouting.main` is the exit ladder; `initializeCli` and
# `initializeDrc` are the two command bodies; the MCP stdio bridge is `// renamed:` to the native
# server; and the API/MCP server halves plus `compareBoardFiles`/`loadBoardFromFile` are rostered
# in `crates/fr-core/src/lib.rs` (Task 0) and cross-referenced from `main.rs`.
Freerouting                 main.rs
Freerouting                 legacy.rs
Freerouting                 logging.rs
Freerouting                 commands/route.rs
Freerouting                 commands/drc.rs
Freerouting                 commands/info.rs
Freerouting                 mcp/stdio.rs

# ── api/mcp/ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ruling AO. Listed one per class rather than left `UNMAPPED`, so a class ADDED to the Java tree
# later shows up as `UNMAPPED` instead of hiding in a glob.
AgentCardController         mcp/server.rs
McpApiKeyValidationFilter   mcp/server.rs
McpApiKeyValidationService  mcp/server.rs
McpApplication              mcp/server.rs
McpContextListener          mcp/server.rs
McpControllerV1             mcp/server.rs
McpControllerV1             mcp/tools/mod.rs
McpRateLimitFilter          mcp/server.rs
McpRealtimeBridge           mcp/stdio.rs
McpWebSocketConfigurator    mcp/stdio.rs
McpWebSocketEndpoint        mcp/stdio.rs
OpenApiMcpToolRegistry      mcp/tools/schema.rs

# ── logger/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Spec §2. Task 5's `logging.rs` carries the `// not ported:` markers and the quirk-AI divergence
# note; `LogEntry`/`LogEntries`/`LogEntryType` reach the manifest through Task 4, not through here.
FRLogger                    logging.rs
Log4j2ConfigurationFactory  logging.rs
LogEntries                  logging.rs
LogEntry                    logging.rs
LogEntryType                logging.rs
TraceEvent                  logging.rs
TraceEventListener          logging.rs
